s><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5818446-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5818446</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1128270A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SFD CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SFD CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>GRAMLICH GABRIELE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAZIMA ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHOJI WATARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TABUCHI DAISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>GRAMLICH, GABRIELE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAZIMA, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHOJI, WATARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TABUCHI, DAISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A user-friendly method is provided for specifying WWW sites. When the user selects any symbol (e.g., word, phrase, sentence, figure and image) and copies it onto clipboard (81) while using an application running on a client computer (3), a resident linker (23) automatically reads the symbol from the clipboard (81) and sends it to a URL server (5). The URL server (5) refers to a database (15), which stores sets of symbols and the corresponding URLs, and supplies the linker (23) with a URL corresponding to the received symbol. A WWW browser (21) accesses the page in the URL and displays it.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé convivial permettant de spécifier des sites Web. Lorsque l'utilisateur sélectionne un symbole quelconque (mot, locution, phrase, figure et image par exemple), et le copie dans son bloc-notes (81), tout en utilisant un application tournant sur un ordinateur client (3), un éditeur (23) de liens résident lit automatiquement le symbole dans le bloc-notes (81) et l'envoie à un serveur (5) URL. Le serveur (5) URL en réfère à une base (15) de données, qui enregistre des ensembles de symboles et leurs URL correspondantes, puis fournit à l'éditeur (23) de liens une URL correspondant au symbole reçu. Un navigateur (21) Web accède à la page de l'URL et procède à son affichage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>